{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction","id":1540885,"title":"The thumbs down emoji reaction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-22T05:17:52-07:00","id":1540885,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon13.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The thumbs down emoji reaction","content":"This is not hugely important, but it's been in the back of my head for awhile now and I'd like to get it out.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one who's kind of bothered by the thumbs down reaction on the forum? I kind of liked when the Like feature was just a binary like or not, but the thumbs down is the one emoji reaction you can drive by and leave that's negative, and I've seen a bunch of them that just kind of leave a sour taste in my mouth. Obviously I don't expect everyone to agree with every post on the forum, but it's one thing to leave a reply expressing your disagreement, and another to just click an I Don't Like It button on the post and move on. I don't know, it feels like a less respectful tone. Is that just me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T10:24:52-07:00","id":1540897,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is just you, but I'm personally torn about this.<br /> <br /> Can't say I think it is a bad thing, despite how bad it is, as I'm not sure if it is a good idea to have every bad sentiment pressed into becoming an actual post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-22-2024, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T10:52:05-07:00","id":1540899,"title":"","content":"It seems to being abused where even the most inoffensive post is getting a thumbs down for no reason and what is the issue that you have? Even if you are not particularly fond of said poster if they post something that is good and sensible or even funny. I can either ignore said post or give props to the statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T12:09:59-07:00","id":1540905,"title":"","content":"I think there's also a problem that the forums just had &quot;like&quot; for such a long time, that there's no forum culture about what the new options actually &quot;mean.&quot;<br /> <br /> Are the &quot;sick&quot; and &quot;angry&quot; reactions something we interpret as an &quot;enhanced like,&quot; that lets us say, &quot;I like your post, but the topic of it upsets me,&quot; or do we interpret them as responses to the poster, &quot;you make me sick/angry for posting that&quot; when we see them used?<br /> <br /> We have no idea if a portion of the thumbs down emotes that seem to have gone up recently are trollish drive-by negativity, or someone that thinks a &quot;thumbs down&quot; to a negative post (like the Vent Thread) is actually a statement of agreeing with the poster instead of how it's taken by most of us as a sign of disagreement (though that doesn't explain some of the uses in the Gush thread... like seriously if there's any thread to not do that in... it's that one).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately they were also just kinda dropped on us randomly during an update with the new (thankfully much better) forum version we're using now. It wasn't a planned roll out where the admins/mods could have taken some time to address how they were expected to be used before people were already using them based on their own preconceptions on how to use them appropriately.<br /> <br /> I don't mind a more robust set of options then just &quot;like.&quot; But I really do wish there was some attempt to make forum expectations on meaning clear so we all know what the default reaction will be treated as. It can be nice to just click an emote instead of writing up a post that's just a duplication of what someone else said, but &quot;like&quot; is the only one with an existing context most forum users here agree on from years of posting together. The rest are currently a source of uncertainty, which can fester.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T14:34:19-07:00","id":1540910,"title":"","content":"One thing I can't understand: what the fuck does a cup of coffee means at all!?<br /> <br /> The other reactions, as much as we don't have a common ground on what they mean, I can make a guess by myself.<br /> <br /> But this cup? I don't have the slightest idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T15:03:14-07:00","id":1540913,"title":"","content":"It's also labeled as &quot;hot beverage&quot; not coffee specifically.<br /> <br /> Very hard to interpret since it's usually a modifier in posts instead of a reaction. It can be anything from, &quot;I feel emotionally warmed by your post like a hot cup of coffee/tea/cocoa/etc.&quot; to an equivalent of a popcorn or sipping wine react, or an encouragement to get someone that's not naming names to &quot;spill the tea&quot; and say the full story in a post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T15:49:39-07:00","id":1540914,"title":"","content":"I left that Hot Beverage reaction because I agree with Heavy Arms' comments about the lack of context for understanding many reactions, the presence of Hot Beverage stood out as most emblematic of this issue, and it also seemed very funny to read through Heavy Arms' post about unclear reaction emoji and see at the end a very unclear reaction emoji.<br /> <br /> No idea why Hot Beverage is in the list to select from. I'm guessing it's possible the forum administrators don't either and that simply came baked in with this iteration of the forum software.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T16:35:59-07:00","id":1540918,"title":"","content":"I figured that the hot beverage was something like that we are hanging out and having drinks and talking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T16:56:49-07:00","id":1540921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1540918#post1540918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured that the hot beverage was something like that we are hanging out and having drinks and talking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's a fair interpretation when using the emoji within your own post. But as a reaction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T20:36:23-07:00","id":1540926,"title":"","content":"When I see someone has given me the Thumbs Down emoji, I like to think that the person is using it in the Roman way, which would mean, &quot;Don't kill this poster,&quot; so it makes me happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T09:54:10-07:00","id":1541398,"title":"","content":"That's a good way to look at it AnubisXy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T04:03:02-07:00","id":1542452,"title":"","content":"I tend to be okay with them. As it avoids a lot if toxicity via replies If i wasnt comfortable with someone disaproving of what i say i wouldnt say it.<br /> <br /> ironically the closest this gets to bothering me is appalling views or dumb takes being upvoted on reddit. For example a catagorically incorrect statement on v5 was thumbed up or far more distirbingly bigotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T12:03:26-07:00","id":1542487,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that I stay away from Reddit in general and social media in general as it's filled with bots and people with really awful or igorant takes on things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T13:20:38-07:00","id":1542494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542452#post1542452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to be okay with them. As it avoids a lot if toxicity via replies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely that.<br /> <br /> We have a company-wide forum at my work. When negative emojis got added as reactions the general toxicity reduced significantly, and reactions like laughing and crying helped to greatly reduce the amount of pointless posts.<br /> <br /> The only reason I\u2019m torn on the issue instead of completely favorable is that in our case every interaction is public: everyone can see who made which reaction. In my experience, this works a lot better than an anonymous reaction. Anyway, it\u2019s a very distinct dynamic because of that, so I can\u2019t say how much my experience translates here (there we have the added aspect that as a company forum, there\u2019s no anonymity at all, for anyone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:10:15-07:00","id":1542571,"title":"","content":"It's a shame we have thumbs down emoji but nobody gives a post to explain the reason for the reason for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:16:51-07:00","id":1542572,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, there seems to be somebody following Satchel around in the CofD forums and anonymously thumbs downing every post they make, which puts a sour taste in my mouth when I see it. Exactly one thumbs down, almost every single post. That just feels petty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:21:06-07:00","id":1542574,"title":"","content":"I know and I see much of the same for my posts in general and yes it's very childish and petty and I see it with a couple of other posters besides Satchel or me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T14:33:02-07:00","id":1542583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542572#post1542572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, there seems to be somebody following Satchel around in the CofD forums and anonymously thumbs downing every post they make, which puts a sour taste in my mouth when I see it. Exactly one thumbs down, almost every single post. That just feels petty.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the reasons I think reactions shouldn't be anonimous.<br /> <br /> But it is what it is, the serial-downvoter is in their right to be petty and childish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T16:29:29-07:00","id":1542591,"title":"","content":"I don't get why someone would do that... don't they have anything better to do then run around here thumbs downing everything? Ugh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T21:47:20-07:00","id":1542747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542591#post1542591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get why someone would do that... don't they have anything better to do then run around here thumbs downing everything? Ugh...</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that prompted me to post about the phenomenon in the Vent thread was coming in one day to find <i>eighteen</i> Notifications of thumbs down reactions, all of them for posts made within the last four years in a single thread. Setting aside the cases where it seems intended to throw extra spice on giving a thumbs up to people who expressed disagreement with me, a bunch of those posts are just non-confrontational answers to questions posed in a thread for asking questions.<br /> <br /> Like, I'd make a joke about how I know I've hit the big time with such a Dedicated Hater\u2122, but this is just kind of annoying, and a substantial portion of that annoyance simply comes from the fact that the Notifications just list the number of reactions the post now has, so there's the tiny extra step of going to the post to see that The Disposable Thumb is at it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T04:13:28-07:00","id":1542760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542747#post1542747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that prompted me to post about the phenomenon in the Vent thread was coming in one day to find <i>eighteen</i> Notifications of thumbs down reactions, all of them for posts made within the last four years in a single thread. Setting aside the cases where it seems intended to throw extra spice on giving a thumbs up to people who expressed disagreement with me, a bunch of those posts are just non-confrontational answers to questions posed in a thread for asking questions.<br /> <br /> Like, I'd make a joke about how I know I've hit the big time with such a Dedicated Hater\u2122, but this is just kind of annoying, and a substantial portion of that annoyance simply comes from the fact that the Notifications just list the number of reactions the post now has, so there's the tiny extra step of going to the post to see that The Disposable Thumb is at it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa... yea, that's super annoying. And the 'Dedicated Hater\u2122' going out of their way to thumbs down years old posts is pretty mental.<br /> <br /> Sorry you're having to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T10:09:05-07:00","id":1542784,"title":"","content":"Can mods still see who makes the reactions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T12:05:35-07:00","id":1542790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542784#post1542784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can mods still see who makes the reactions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. I do think if they can, Satchel's particular case may warrant intervention, because that much is true: most of the Mystery Thumbsdown happens to technical responses in a technical thread, it couldn't be farther from anything polemic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T02:58:24-07:00","id":1542812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542572#post1542572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, there seems to be somebody following Satchel around in the CofD forums and anonymously thumbs downing every post they make, which puts a sour taste in my mouth when I see it. Exactly one thumbs down, almost every single post. That just feels petty.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair it more strongly reflects on whose doing it being a loser.<br /> <br /> <br /> I had it going on with white wolf reddit once. It was pretty obvious who it was. Probably part of working in a rough urban school but low level insults no longer bother.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pARFcJQclCc?si=vXMGfM_BWA6O8M2e\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pARFcJQclCc?si=vXMGfM_BWA6O8M2e\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pARFcJQclCc?si=vXMGfM_BWA6O8M2e\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/pARFcJQclCc?si=vXMGfM_BWA6O8M2e </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-28-2024, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T12:57:53-07:00","id":1542834,"title":"","content":"I'm sure that Satchel can make a statement to the moderators of these boards and can take quick action against the thumbs down poster whom seems to have a personal dislike towards Satchel for reasons I can't guess as there is nothing in the posts that warrant it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T12:59:32-07:00","id":1542835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542790#post1542790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good question. I do think if they can, Satchel's particular case may warrant intervention, because that much is true: most of the Mystery Thumbsdown happens to technical responses in a technical thread, it couldn't be farther from anything polemic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure they can as they would have special aminstration duties and there is no such thing as anoyomity on the message boards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T23:06:32-07:00","id":1542855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542834#post1542834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure that Satchel can make a statement to the moderators of these boards and can take quick action against the thumbs down poster whom seems to have a personal dislike towards Satchel for reasons I can't guess as there is nothing in the posts that warrant it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to be negative about this, buuuuuuuut<br /> <br /> What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">forum rule</a> would this spamming be considered against?<br /> <br /> XX not withstanding, unless the mods can also see the time reactions are done in and can prove said poster is essentially flooding Satchel's* notifications with negative reactions, you basically just have evidence that people don't like the post, or maybe even the person-and while that can be sour for any conversation where good faith readings, interpretations, and arguments are otherwise being made, there's nothing saying you're not allowed to dislike a person, or even be vocal about it, so long as it's decently respectful in the terms of the rest of the rules. If it doesn't have the time stamp, basically whoever is doing it can basically just say they have a long history of disliking Satchel's takes, and even admitting to some pettiness and negatively reacting to his posts because it's him.<br /> <br /> Now of course, XX is there FOR stuff like this, but it's a tricky line to cut where it's harassment (if the mods can legit feel comfortable calling it that, because that can set their precedent for this sort of thing moving forward) and where people are allowed to basically have a bad opinion of a post or a person so long as it meets the criteria for engagement, no matter how otherwise faulty the reasons for that can be.<br /> <br /> Arguably the sheer volume of it could considered a form of threadcrapping, particularly if it's adjoined with any thread necromancy, but I think part of the reason the person doing this (if they are deliberately doing it and not just siccing a bot with a loose set of parameters on the forums) is doing this particular thing is because it's kind of small enough that it's hard to justify moderator action against it, particularly since it has a certain level of infrequency.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying this because I don't think anything should be done-certainly not because it doesn't affect me, because it seems like any time I come back here to do any kind of post, I end up with a similar deluge-I'm just not sure how grounded the response can be.<br /> <br /> *I use Satchel here because he has become our icon for this issue recently, but assume I am using him as an iconic for everyone who feels particularly belaboured by this shit, so insert your name or the name of someone you're bummed about getting this treatment here as need be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T22:17:13-07:00","id":1542893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542855#post1542855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to be negative about this, buuuuuuuut<br /> <br /> What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">forum rule</a> would this spamming be considered against?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Rule 1.<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, it is demonstrably out of proportion and recurrent against a specific poster, this is harassment and goes directly against rule 1. Sure, no one is required to like no one else, but by the very first rule you ARE required to respect even those you dislike.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re right that it also requires attention to timestamps for us to have a strong case, but the forums do have such timestamps. When a reaction is made, the poster is informed of this by a notification with a timestamp.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I\u2019m on board with being worried about how this would be applied. I do think we need to be cautious on how to classify a streak of actions as harassment, and even more about the specific actions to be taken in such a case. All that assuming the moderators have access to the salient information to begin with.<br /> <br /> That said, Satchel\u2019s case specifically is, or has been until recently, the poster child of one in which something being done is warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T09:04:34-07:00","id":1542913,"title":"","content":"Ngl, I keep getting hit with a bunch of random thumbs down a lot as well. Not sure if it's the same person going after Satchel or someone else, but I figured it'd be worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> I tend to just ignore it and go on with my day, but it is weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T12:51:18-07:00","id":1542925,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking the same thing Matt as I have had random thumbs down for posts that are not even remotely polarizing. In this case Satchel has a strong case as someone is giving thumbs down reactions to even very old threads that are inactive or very general posts about game play mechanics such as how Dark Decree works in the VTR board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-30-2024, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T15:39:18-07:00","id":1543220,"title":"","content":"It seems like that we have been given a break from the thumbs down troll as I haven't any for Satchel, Matt or me for that matter. Maybe the moderators noticed the issue and took steps to curb the abuse or the poster is on vacation.<br /> <br /> I spoke to soon as the thumbs down poster is back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-06-2024, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T16:28:59-07:00","id":1543557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1542572#post1542572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, there seems to be somebody following Satchel around in the CofD forums and anonymously thumbs downing every post they make, which puts a sour taste in my mouth when I see it. Exactly one thumbs down, almost every single post. That just feels petty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OH I agree that it does leave a bad taste in everyone's mouth when they see getting thumbs down for no reason.<br /> <br /> For instance I don't know how my post on Furioso where for the most part I enjoyed the film. But my only critic was that seeing Chris Hemsworth still looking shredded in a post apocalyptic setting takes me out of the experience.<br /> <br /> For that I get a thumbs down by this person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T08:27:34-08:00","id":1548359,"title":"","content":"It's possible that the thumbs down person is back again haunting the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T04:18:23-08:00","id":1548399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction?p=1548359#post1548359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible that the thumbs down person is back again haunting the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh... sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T12:00:56-08:00","id":1548404,"title":"","content":"If it gets worse, the moderator will be notified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T12:14:10-07:00","id":1551594,"title":"","content":"So far so good as the thumbs down poster isn't bothering anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T15:20:34-07:00","id":1551693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1540885-the-thumbs-down-emoji-reaction#post1540885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not hugely important, but it's been in the back of my head for awhile now and I'd like to get it out.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one who's kind of bothered by the thumbs down reaction on the forum? I kind of liked when the Like feature was just a binary like or not, but the thumbs down is the one emoji reaction you can drive by and leave that's negative, and I've seen a bunch of them that just kind of leave a sour taste in my mouth. Obviously I don't expect everyone to agree with every post on the forum, but it's one thing to leave a reply expressing your disagreement, and another to just click an I Don't Like It button on the post and move on. I don't know, it feels like a less respectful tone. Is that just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I soooo was going to give you a thumbs-down; but the thumbs down really belongs on say, news-forums when you're talking politics as a way to disagree. If I disagree on here, I might post about it, or I might not; who cares it's a hobby gaming-forum. If someone posts a rule I don't like, I don't use it in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}